<title>SWEDEN: LATVIA - SKANSKA TO BUILD RIGA SHOPPING CENTER.</title>
<headline>LATVIA - SKANSKA TO BUILD RIGA SHOPPING CENTER.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company Skanska said on Friday it would build a shopping center in Riga, project valued at $19 million.</p>
<p>&quot;An agreement on financing the project -- an investment for Skanska and the city of Riga of $19 million -- was signed today by Skanska International Building, the European Bank of UTVECKLING Reconstruction and Swedish Export Credit,&quot; said Skanska in a statement.</p>
<p>The center will have 9,000 square meters of shop and office space and will be finalised in the second half of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Jorgen Osterberg, Stockholm newsroom +46 8 700 1007</p>
